# The build context is the repository, and these are the parts of it that an
# image has no use for. `.git` is the large one -- the history is not in the
# image, and copying it would bust the layer cache on every commit; `.venv*`
# would be a host's interpreter copied over the image's own, and `docs/images`
# is the README's screenshots, which no command in the image reads.
.git
.gitignore
.venv*
docs/images
# Build and test residue from a host build of the same tree.
**/__pycache__
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
